elan: retry the capture when the sensor is not ready or the finger was lifted

After the pre-scan command the driver expects 0x55 (finger present). Some sensors answer 0x00
(not ready) or 0xaf (finger removed / busy); 0x0c58 already retries on these values. 04f3:0c4f
(Acer Aspire 7 A715-42G) sends them too, typically after the first enroll stage when the finger
is lifted, and every enroll ended with "protocol error" / enroll-disconnected. Retry on these
values for all sensors and log the unexpected value.

--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
@@ -557,15 +557,17 @@
           fpi_image_device_report_finger_status (idev, TRUE);
           elan_run_cmd (ssm, dev, &get_image_cmd, ELAN_CMD_TIMEOUT);
         }
-      else if (self->dev_type == ELAN_0C58 && self->last_read &&
+      else if (self->last_read &&
                (self->last_read[0] == 0x00 || self->last_read[0] == 0xaf))
         {
           /* 0x00 - not ready
-           * 0xaf - finger removed or sensor busy (seen on 0x0c58) */
+           * 0xaf - finger removed or sensor busy (seen on 0x0c58 and 0x0c4f) */
           fpi_ssm_jump_to_state_delayed (ssm, CAPTURE_WAIT_FINGER, 10);
         }
       else
         {
+          if (self->last_read)
+            fp_dbg ("unexpected pre-scan response 0x%02x", self->last_read[0]);
           /* XXX: The timeout is emulated incorrectly, resulting in a zero byte read. */
           if (fpi_device_emulation_mode_enabled (FP_DEVICE (self)))
             fpi_ssm_mark_completed (ssm);
